PARITY NOTES (web -> native)
  • Data: web reads `useVehicles()[0]` as the sample vehicle then `useDriveScore(vid)`
    (GET /drives/score?vehicle_id=). Native binds the same via the P1/S8
    `DriveScoreGaugeSource` seam (production wraps the shared useVehicles + useDriveScore
    holders) — NO HTTP in the view.
  • scoreColor: >=80 excellent, >=60 good, >=40 fair, else poor — reproduced as DriveScoreZone
    and unit-asserted at the 40/60/80 thresholds; mapped to the SI status tokens
    (success / info[cyan, web #22d3ee] / warning / danger) so it tracks light/dark/high-contrast.
  • Gauge: web RadialGauge value=overall(clamp 0..100), label=grade, unit="Weekly score".
    Native ring shows overall + grade in-center and "Weekly score" as the caption (Apple HIG);
    overall clamp + whole/fractional decimals + grade `?? '—'` fallback unit-asserted.
  • Sub-scores: web `stats` row (Efficiency/Smoothness/Speed Discipline) + the `isTall`
    `MetricBar`s — both reproduced; values `?? 0`, integer readouts via fmtInt, per-bar tint
    via scoreColor(value); order pinned [efficiency, smoothness, speed].
  • Responsive: web `isCompact = cols===1 && rows===1` -> ring only; `isTall = rows>=2` ->
    ring + stat row + metric bars. Both branches implemented + size-clamped to min/max.
  • States: web `WidgetShell` loading(skeleton)/error(QueryError+retry) + body content/
